  "id": "stereoscopic-depth-perception",
  "term": "stereoscopic depth perception",
  "definition": "Stereoscopic depth perception is seeing depth from the differences between the two eyes’ views, especially from how surface structure is differently patterned across the images. It appears to depend more on higher-order disparities in intensity, texture, and motion that reflect local surface shape than on simple mismatches of retinal position alone.",
